MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Ashes Of The Wake and The War Within combine forceful riffs with precision and melody, which connects closely with my listening to In Flames, Soilwork, and Advance And Vanquish.",
    "Iowa fits the aggressive side of my taste reflected in Ten Thousand Fists and my heavier listening, making it a compelling choice today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger offers heaviness, but its raw, clattering sound misses the layered arrangements and precise guitar work I want right now.",
    "War on Errorism's punk sound does not connect with my current metal mood. Meteora and Hybrid Theory fit my melodic rock taste, but they are less compelling than the heavier options this visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat aggression and heaviness as enough to make albums equally appealing, although the way the riffs and melodies work together matters to me.",
    "My broader rock listening seems to carry too much weight for this visit, when I am choosing more selectively around heavier guitar-driven music."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated listening to In Flames and Soilwork points toward a particular combination of melody, intricate riffs, and controlled aggression.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I would choose today: dark grooves or melodic hooks alone are less compelling right now than precise, varied guitar work."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy music but only partly capture why precise riffs, melody, and layered aggression make certain albums stronger choices today."
}
